From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernardo Pereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:33:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Project non-perspective 3d transforms onto the plane

A transform list that mentions a 3d function was dropped entirely, so
`rotateX(45deg)` and `matrix3d(...)` left the box untransformed. Outside a 3d
rendering context the transform still applies as a painting effect, and without
perspective the z = 0 plane projects to exactly the 2d affine part of the
matrix (e.g. `rotateX(45deg)` on a 20px box projects to 14.142px tall at
y = 2.929).

A matrix with perspective (m14/m24) is still dropped: its projection is
projective, not affine.
---
 src/stylo_to_kurbo.rs | 26 +++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/stylo_to_kurbo.rs b/src/stylo_to_kurbo.rs
index dc12a66..9ea1e12 100644
--- a/src/stylo_to_kurbo.rs
+++ b/src/stylo_to_kurbo.rs
@@ -65,15 +65,23 @@ pub fn resolve_2d_transform(
             // matrix needs 3d: `translate3d(x, y, 0)` sets it while resolving to a
             // plain 2d translation.
             //
-            // TODO: support 3D transforms. Outside a 3d rendering context the spec
-            // still applies the transform as a painting effect -- its own example
-            // paints `rotateY(50deg)` narrower -- so dropping one is wrong. `is_2d()`
-            // is closer than the flag, not the rule.
+            // Outside a 3d rendering context the transform still applies as a painting
+            // effect -- the spec's own example paints `rotateY(50deg)` narrower -- so a
+            // 3d matrix is only dropped when it cannot be expressed on the z = 0 plane.
+            // Without perspective the projected position of that plane is exactly the
+            // 2d affine part; with it the projection is projective, not affine.
             // See: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transforms-2/#3d-transform-rendering
-            .filter(|(t, _has_3d)| t.is_2d())
-            .map(|(t, _)| {
-                // See: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transforms-2/#two-dimensional-subset
-                // And https://docs.rs/kurbo/latest/kurbo/struct.Affine.html#method.new
-                Affine::new([t.m11, t.m12, t.m21, t.m22, t.m41, t.m42].map(|v| v as f64))
+            .and_then(|(t, _has_3d)| {
+                if t.m14 == 0.0 && t.m24 == 0.0 && t.m44 == 1.0 {
+                    // See: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transforms-2/#two-dimensional-subset
+                    // And https://docs.rs/kurbo/latest/kurbo/struct.Affine.html#method.new
+                    Some(Affine::new(
+                        [t.m11, t.m12, t.m21, t.m22, t.m41, t.m42].map(|v| v as f64),
+                    ))
+                } else {
+                    // TODO: support perspective, where the projected plane needs a
+                    // projective map rather than an affine one.
+                    None
+                }
             })
     };
